    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 1205 by French crusaders, it was the most durable <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> state created in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>.</li><li>A model feudal society of twelve baronies, its customs were codified in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assizes-of-romania">Assizes of Romania</a>.</li><li>Defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pelagonia">Pelagonia</a> in 1259 cost it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mystras">Mistras</a>, the base from which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> reconquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> by 1432.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Venetian writer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marino-sanudo-torsello">Marino Sanudo Torsello</a> reported that at the princes’ court in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> French was spoken as well as in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

