onnese">Peloponnese</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1259</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-villehardouin">William II</a> is captured at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pelagonia">Battle of Pelagonia</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1262</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mystras">Mistras</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monemvasia">Monemvasia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-magne">Grand Magne</a> are ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1267</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-viterbo-1267">Treaty of Viterbo</a> places <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles of Anjou</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1316</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-of-majorca">Ferdinand of Majorca</a> is killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manolada">Battle of Manolada</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1432</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-palaiologos">Thomas Palaiologos</a> annexes the last of the principality</span></li></ol>
